{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Awesome things</b> — the meaning: when the nations serve HaShem, they dwell securely, without fear of enemy or hunger. And the meaning: when we are in awe, then You answer us to save us." "And the meaning of <b>in righteousness</b> — as if it were written 'in Your righteousness,' or 'in the righteousness that we repented,' and You atoned for our transgressions. Rabbi Moses said: <b>the trust of all the ends of the earth</b> — 'all' refers to men, as in 'and all the earth came to Egypt' (Genesis 41:57), and men who are far away, and the meaning is that You save them though they are at the ends of the earth and at sea, and there is no human ability to save them. And in my opinion: because the ends of every body are not bodies themselves, as in 'who creates the ends of the earth' (Proverbs 30:4)." "And the meaning of <b>and the distant sea</b> — because half the globe of the earth is seas, and he said 'distant' because they are many."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:44.941198363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}